---
/** Static, hand-written -- never passes through the content pipeline. See
 *  NEEDS-HUMAN-REVIEW.md "Liveliness Spec" §5: the one page on the site
 *  with a first-person voice ("Who built it" below), because the honesty
 *  the site can't get from claiming human experience in its own content
 *  has to come from somewhere -- saying plainly what the site is. */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/site-config';
import { aboutSourcesFor } from '../lib/about-sources';

const isBrookings = siteConfig.townId === 'brookings_sd';
const sources = aboutSourcesFor(siteConfig.townId);
---
<BaseLayout title={`About — ${siteConfig.siteName}`}
  description={`What ${siteConfig.siteName} is, how it's made, and who built it.`}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About {siteConfig.siteName}</h1>

    {isBrookings ? (
      <p>Brookings Register, the town's newspaper, closed in August 2025. Since
      then, there's been no single place to find out what the city council
      decided, what's happening at the library this week, or when the Jackrabbits
      play next. {siteConfig.siteName} is an attempt to fill that gap: a local
      news site for Brookings, assembled automatically from public sources --
      city and county meeting agendas, the library and city calendars, and
      official alerts.</p>
    ) : (
      <p>Local newspapers have been closing or shrinking all over the country,
      and small and mid-sized cities are often the first places to lose the
      kind of coverage that keeps residents in the loop. {siteConfig.siteName}
      is an attempt to give {siteConfig.cityName} a single place to find out
      what's happening: a local news site assembled automatically from public
      sources -- city meeting agendas, the library and city calendars, county
      records, and official alerts.</p>
    )}

    <h2>How it is made</h2>
    <p>Software checks the sources listed below on a schedule -- most hourly,
    some daily or monthly depending on how often they change. New items are
    summarized in plain language by an AI language model, working only from
    what those sources say, and published without a person reviewing each one
    first.</p>
    <p>That means no one is reporting from the ground here. Nothing on this
    site is a firsthand account -- no one attended the meeting, walked the
    site, or talked to anyone involved. Every summary is a machine-written
    digest of a public document or feed, always linked back to that original
    source so you can read the full thing yourself. Read the full,
    source-by-source breakdown on <a href="/how-we-gather-this/">how we
    gather this</a>.</p>

    <h2>What you won't find here</h2>
    <p>{siteConfig.siteName} doesn't cover arrests, court records, or obituaries.
    That's a deliberate choice, not an oversight: this site exists to tell you
    what's happening in your town, not to follow anyone through a hard moment
    in their life. If you're looking for that kind of coverage, you won't find
    it — by design.</p>

    <h2>Who built it</h2>
    <p>I'm one person, building this in my spare time outside a day job,
    because {siteConfig.cityName} didn't have a site like it. I'm not a
    journalist and I don't live in {siteConfig.cityName} -- I write software,
    from Sweden, and this is what that looks like pointed at local news. I'd
    rather say that plainly than dress up an automated site with a fake
    masthead.</p>

    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p>Everything on this site traces back to one of these, checked on a
    schedule and never altered beyond the plain-language summary:</p>
    <ul class="sources">
      {sources.map((s) => (
        <li><a href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.name}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Automated summaries occasionally get something wrong. Errors are
    corrected as soon as they're reported -- <a href="/contact/">use the
    contact form</a> to flag one.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.prose { max-width: 38rem; }
.prose h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
.prose p { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
.sources { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding-left: 1.25rem; }
.sources li { margin: 0.25rem 0; }
</style>
